  "body": "Sea views, generous accommodation and space to enjoy life together make this Torbay home an appealing choice for families ready for their next chapter. With five bedrooms, four bathrooms including three ensuites, and a separate guest toilet, there is room for a growing household, visiting relatives and everyone's daily routine.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home, the kitchen connects with the open-plan dining and living areas, creating a welcoming setting for family meals and entertaining. Whether you are hosting friends for dinner or enjoying a quiet evening at home, the layout offers space to gather comfortably.\r\n\r\nMultiple living areas give the family freedom to spread out. Come together downstairs, enjoy a quieter moment in the upstairs lounge or step onto the adjoining deck for some fresh air. The sea views bring an extra dimension to the home's coastal appeal.\r\n\r\nFive bedrooms provide flexibility for different stages of family life, with three ensuite bedrooms offering added privacy and convenience. The ground-floor accommodation and adjoining bathroom are particularly useful for guests or extended family, while the remaining bedrooms upstairs keep everyone comfortably connected. A separate laundry and double garage complete the practical essentials.\r\n\r\nThe wider location adds plenty to enjoy. Discover the cafés and shops of Torbay Village, spend time beside the water at Waiake Beach or head to Long Bay Regional Park for beach days, picnics and coastal walks. Browns Bay offers further dining and shopping options, while Albany provides access to larger retail centres and transport connections.\r\n\r\nFor families seeking sea views, versatile accommodation and the lifestyle of Auckland's coastal North Shore, this home brings together plenty of reasons to make a move.\r\n\r\nContact us today to arrange your viewing or visit our next open home.",
